# Q57 with Q59 (K03a): inside a definition a KNOWN head is a call, checked against the resolved value's contract --
# Known is an ordinary named Structure with no arguments, so `Known(1)` in C's body is the arity refusal, where it
# stands; neither a nested definition nor a fallback.
Known:
    size_t: x 1U
end: Known
C: Known(1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
